WEBVTT

00:01:32.641 --> 00:01:34.852
" Episode 6
Rotten Repose "

00:01:34.852 --> 00:01:36.895
" Episode 6 Rotten
Repose " Okay, lift it up!

00:01:36.895 --> 00:01:36.979
Okay, lift it up!

00:01:57.666 --> 00:01:59.209
Up! Up!

00:03:01.730 --> 00:03:04.274
There. Overhaul complete.

00:03:05.275 --> 00:03:06.568
I 'm worn out.

00:03:06.777 --> 00:03:08.904
Now it's as good as new.

00:03:10.447 --> 00:03:13.200
But what about the paint job?

00:03:14.952 --> 00:03:19.206
True. lt's not picturesque this way.

00:03:20.541 --> 00:03:22.292
I 've already decided about that.

00:03:35.973 --> 00:03:38.684
Looks kind of weak.

00:03:38.892 --> 00:03:40.561
That's not true.

00:03:40.769 --> 00:03:43.313
They're the colors of the mech l used to pilot.

00:03:43.522 --> 00:03:44.231
Huh?

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:47.735
I know this is arbitrary,
but l 'd like to call it Al the Second.

00:03:47.943 --> 00:03:49.403
What's up with that?

00:03:54.032 --> 00:03:55.367
Is that weird?

00:04:03.417 --> 00:04:06.795
The winner, Stick Man!

00:04:09.757 --> 00:04:12.301
It's our turn!
Are final adjustments done?!

00:04:12.509 --> 00:04:13.761
Okay!

00:04:15.721 --> 00:04:16.930
Done!

00:04:18.223 --> 00:04:20.225
Be careful, Sousuke.

00:04:25.647 --> 00:04:28.066
Okay, Sousuke, it's up to you!

00:04:28.275 --> 00:04:29.485
No problem.

00:04:44.249 --> 00:04:48.754
Next bout, category: <i>Melee</i> Weapons.

00:04:48.962 --> 00:04:51.381
Crossbow!

00:04:51.590 --> 00:04:55.594
Operator, Sohsky Seagull!

00:04:56.762 --> 00:04:57.930
Vanguard!

00:04:58.138 --> 00:05:02.434
Operator, John C. Bogle!

00:05:02.643 --> 00:05:03.727
Pight!

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:21.703
The winner, Crossbow!

00:05:27.501 --> 00:05:28.669
--Sousuke! Wow! Amazing!
--Well done!

00:05:28.669 --> 00:05:30.170
--Sousuke! Wow! Amazing!
--Awesome!

00:05:31.547 --> 00:05:33.006
You 're the real deal!

00:05:33.215 --> 00:05:35.133
Mm-hm!

00:05:35.342 --> 00:05:38.220
But maybe the match was a little too short?

00:05:38.428 --> 00:05:39.555
What're you saying?

00:05:39.763 --> 00:05:41.640
He just needs to win!

00:05:41.849 --> 00:05:44.434
That's right. l just need to win.

00:05:45.978 --> 00:05:46.937
Right, right.

00:05:47.145 --> 00:05:48.188
It sure was quick.

00:05:48.397 --> 00:05:51.567
--You 're really skilled. l mean, wow!
--Hey, Sousuke, how are you so good at this?

00:05:52.734 --> 00:05:53.819
Pight!

00:06:00.742 --> 00:06:03.829
The winner, Crossbow!

00:06:14.506 --> 00:06:15.591
Pight!

00:06:25.267 --> 00:06:28.604
The winner, Crossbow!

00:07:01.053 --> 00:07:02.179
Go!

00:07:13.982 --> 00:07:16.693
The winner, Crossbow!

00:07:18.528 --> 00:07:19.613
He did it.

00:07:20.572 --> 00:07:21.949
He's won every time.

00:07:22.157 --> 00:07:24.201
Who the hell is this guy?

00:07:24.409 --> 00:07:28.413
Does it really matter?
His strength is a huge help.

00:07:31.875 --> 00:07:33.251
You 're knocking them dead out there.

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:35.212
No, none of them died.

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:36.463
Weirdo.

00:07:36.672 --> 00:07:38.340
I am?

00:07:38.548 --> 00:07:42.386
But seriously, you haven 't
even broken a sweat.

00:07:44.262 --> 00:07:46.306
My body must be used to it.

00:07:47.349 --> 00:07:51.937
"The AS is an extension of
the trained soldier's body. "

00:07:52.145 --> 00:07:54.731
Or so it was written. ls it true?

00:07:54.940 --> 00:07:56.233
What's up with that?

00:07:56.441 --> 00:07:58.110
I 've been studying up lately.

00:07:58.318 --> 00:08:02.197
What you said is the motto of
the SAS Assault Cavalry Team.

00:08:02.406 --> 00:08:04.574
What's the SAS?

00:08:04.783 --> 00:08:06.576
A British special forces unit.

00:08:06.785 --> 00:08:08.412
Don 't tell me you were with them?

00:08:08.620 --> 00:08:11.748
No, but my superior officer was.

00:08:15.252 --> 00:08:17.212
What am l doing?

00:08:17.421 --> 00:08:18.213
What?

00:08:18.422 --> 00:08:20.132
No, never mind.

00:08:21.842 --> 00:08:25.512
Man, you are full of mysteries.

00:08:29.850 --> 00:08:30.892
What?

00:08:31.101 --> 00:08:35.439
It's like, l ' m not sure why...

00:08:35.647 --> 00:08:37.691
...but are you anxious about something?

00:08:37.899 --> 00:08:39.443
That's not...

00:08:42.070 --> 00:08:43.655
That might be true.

00:08:43.864 --> 00:08:45.490
Why?

00:08:45.699 --> 00:08:47.576
Because l feel comfortable <i>here.</i>

00:08:47.784 --> 00:08:49.286
It's baffling.

00:08:49.494 --> 00:08:50.662
Here, as in...?

00:08:50.871 --> 00:08:52.122
With you.

00:08:53.290 --> 00:08:55.333
L-l don 't know what you mean.

00:08:55.542 --> 00:08:58.545
Why's it a problem that you ' re comfortable?

00:09:05.719 --> 00:09:07.554
Here, today's pay.

00:09:08.555 --> 00:09:09.765
That's a big help.

00:09:09.973 --> 00:09:12.601
Well, you kicked butt.

00:09:16.271 --> 00:09:18.982
Somebody's in love, no doubt about it.

00:09:19.191 --> 00:09:21.151
Who is? With whom?

00:09:21.359 --> 00:09:24.112
Isn 't it obvious? Nami is, with you.

00:09:24.321 --> 00:09:27.199
Oh. That's only natural.

00:09:27.407 --> 00:09:29.534
Those are bold words, lad!

00:09:29.743 --> 00:09:33.914
My operator skills are extremely high
by this city's standards.

00:09:34.122 --> 00:09:38.293
Nami is a team owner.
Of course she values <i>me.</i>

00:09:39.419 --> 00:09:40.754
--Por real?
--<i>Jeez...</i>

00:09:40.962 --> 00:09:43.507
No, that's not what l meant.

00:09:43.715 --> 00:09:46.134
As a girl, that is.

00:09:46.343 --> 00:09:48.929
She may not look it,
but she's got strong morals.

00:09:49.137 --> 00:09:52.140
Lots of guys have made passes at her,
but she turned them all down.

00:09:52.349 --> 00:09:55.852
That's right. Kaew, you were one of them.

00:09:56.061 --> 00:09:58.021
Damn it! Don 't tell people that!

00:09:58.230 --> 00:10:02.067
Whenever she shows up and
you 're not here, she's sure to ask:

00:10:02.275 --> 00:10:03.777
"Where's Sousuke?"

00:10:03.985 --> 00:10:08.031
--She's all blunt!
--Really blunt! So blunt it's suspicious.

00:10:09.533 --> 00:10:11.034
She doesn 't ask about Lemon.

00:10:13.203 --> 00:10:14.329
What about you?

00:10:14.538 --> 00:10:15.539
What do you mean?

00:10:15.747 --> 00:10:17.290
I mean Nami.

00:10:17.499 --> 00:10:18.917
How do you feel about her?

00:10:20.752 --> 00:10:21.586
Chidori.

00:10:21.795 --> 00:10:23.213
--Huh?
--Nothing.

00:10:23.421 --> 00:10:25.590
Things seem kinda serious.

00:10:25.799 --> 00:10:28.135
Did you leave a girl behind
back home, or something?

00:10:28.343 --> 00:10:30.303
It's the reverse.

00:10:30.512 --> 00:10:32.430
What do you mean "the reverse" ?

00:10:32.639 --> 00:10:33.056
Whoops.

00:10:33.265 --> 00:10:37.811
Lunch break's over, guys.
Now, back to work.

00:10:38.019 --> 00:10:39.312
You got it.

00:10:39.521 --> 00:10:40.981
Here, Sousuke.

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:42.774
What's this?

00:10:42.983 --> 00:10:46.403
A shopping list.
You and Lemon go buy this stuff.

00:10:47.404 --> 00:10:49.781
It's nearly all specialized AS parts.

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:52.200
You can 't get these at a regular shop.

00:10:52.409 --> 00:10:55.787
Oh? You haven 't been to the market yet?

00:10:55.996 --> 00:10:57.080
Market?

00:11:06.756 --> 00:11:08.717
It's just like Akihabara.

00:11:08.925 --> 00:11:10.969
Isn 't that Japan 's Porn Town?

00:11:11.178 --> 00:11:12.971
No, Electric Town.

00:11:13.180 --> 00:11:14.681
Oh, okay.

00:11:17.642 --> 00:11:20.478
A BM D chip is $400?!

00:11:20.687 --> 00:11:21.563
Is that expensive?

00:11:21.771 --> 00:11:24.524
The opposite. They were $2,000 a year ago.

00:11:24.733 --> 00:11:27.903
Huh, then they've really dropped in price.

00:11:28.111 --> 00:11:30.697
Just goes to show how
commonplace ASes have become.

00:11:30.906 --> 00:11:33.033
Even so, it's remarkable.

00:11:33.241 --> 00:11:34.743
It's hard to put into words,

00:11:34.951 --> 00:11:37.037
but the rate at which
they' re spreading is strange.

00:11:38.038 --> 00:11:40.498
Or maybe l 'm overthinking this.

00:11:40.707 --> 00:11:42.042
Maybe.

00:11:42.250 --> 00:11:43.418
That's rude.

00:11:43.627 --> 00:11:45.045
Yeah, well.

00:11:45.253 --> 00:11:47.714
I am still something of an artist.

00:11:47.923 --> 00:11:48.882
Artist...

00:11:49.090 --> 00:11:52.469
That's why l ' m curious. About your art.

00:11:53.470 --> 00:11:55.889
I mean the way you fight.

00:11:56.097 --> 00:12:00.393
It doesn 't feel like skill. lt's art.

00:12:00.602 --> 00:12:01.645
Art...

00:12:01.853 --> 00:12:03.605
This is what comes to mind
when l watch your matches.

00:12:03.813 --> 00:12:08.026
You 're not simply fighting to earn a living.

00:12:08.235 --> 00:12:10.028
You 're fighting for something bigger...

00:12:10.237 --> 00:12:12.948
Some goal, off in the distance.

00:12:13.156 --> 00:12:17.869
I 'm a layman when it comes to ASes,
but l just get that kind of feeling.

00:12:18.078 --> 00:12:18.912
How about it?

00:12:19.120 --> 00:12:21.373
I 'm not sure. But...

00:12:21.581 --> 00:12:22.666
But?

00:12:22.874 --> 00:12:25.961
When it comes to ways of
expressing myself well, this is all l have.

00:12:26.169 --> 00:12:27.170
Combat?

00:12:27.379 --> 00:12:28.922
That's right.

00:12:29.130 --> 00:12:34.427
I wish l had some talent like
photography, or music, or drawing.

00:12:34.636 --> 00:12:36.846
But unfortunately, this is all l 've got.

00:12:38.098 --> 00:12:40.308
Don 't sell yourself short.

00:12:40.517 --> 00:12:42.769
You might be surprised to find
you have some other talent.

00:12:42.978 --> 00:12:44.312
Por instance...

00:12:44.521 --> 00:12:45.647
Por instance?

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:48.817
Like being a ladies' man.

00:12:49.025 --> 00:12:50.527
What the heck?

00:12:52.737 --> 00:12:53.738
Don 't move!

00:12:55.740 --> 00:12:58.451
Get down on your knees! Slowly!

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:00.161
Uh, officer?

00:13:00.370 --> 00:13:02.122
L-l think this is probably some mis--

00:13:02.330 --> 00:13:03.206
Ouickly!

00:13:03.415 --> 00:13:06.918
Wh-Which is it, quickly or slowly?

00:13:07.127 --> 00:13:08.169
Ow!

00:13:16.052 --> 00:13:22.350
We got a report that two
young foreigners were stealing.

00:13:23.560 --> 00:13:25.770
It was based on reliable information.

00:13:25.979 --> 00:13:27.814
Wh-What are you talking about?!

00:13:28.023 --> 00:13:31.192
You pretended not to know <i>anything</i>
when that Rick guy got killed!

00:13:31.401 --> 00:13:32.402
Lemon! Cut it out!

00:13:32.610 --> 00:13:35.363
You 've got to be kidding!
This is a human rights violation!

00:13:35.572 --> 00:13:36.740
I want a lawyer immedi--

00:13:36.948 --> 00:13:38.992
You should shut up, foreigner.

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:41.244
And who are you?

00:13:41.453 --> 00:13:45.040
The police chief.
That's all you need to know.

00:13:45.248 --> 00:13:47.917
Good, that's easy to remember.

00:13:48.126 --> 00:13:49.794
You 've got guts.

00:13:50.003 --> 00:13:53.631
But if you cop an insolent attitude
with me in this city...

00:13:56.885 --> 00:14:01.848
...you ' ll wish you hadn 't, Sousuke Sagara.

00:14:13.193 --> 00:14:15.153
You! Get out here!

00:14:15.362 --> 00:14:16.446
Sousuke!

00:14:16.654 --> 00:14:17.989
Don 't worry.

00:14:23.161 --> 00:14:24.496
A tooth?

00:14:26.081 --> 00:14:31.294
Robbery, assault, attempted
murder, extortion, perjury,

00:14:31.503 --> 00:14:34.881
illegal immigration,
obstruction of police duties,

00:14:35.090 --> 00:14:38.676
possession and use of an illegal weapon.

00:14:40.762 --> 00:14:42.847
Do you have any other requests?

00:14:43.056 --> 00:14:44.224
What are you talking about?

00:14:44.432 --> 00:14:45.975
Your list of charges.

00:14:46.184 --> 00:14:50.647
How about assaulting a police chief?
l 'll do that one right now.

00:14:54.067 --> 00:14:56.611
You don 't seem to get it.

00:14:56.820 --> 00:15:02.242
This isn 't just an interrogation room.
lt's also a courtroom.

00:15:02.450 --> 00:15:07.497
I 'm both the prosecutor and the judge.
And the executor of punishment, too.

00:15:07.705 --> 00:15:10.166
You must be quite understaffed.

00:15:10.917 --> 00:15:14.838
What do you want? Did you come here
just to tell me my prison term?

00:15:15.046 --> 00:15:19.509
You 're sharp. As you guessed,
this is about the arena.

00:15:19.717 --> 00:15:21.719
You 're on a winning streak, aren 't you?

00:15:21.928 --> 00:15:23.346
What about it?

00:15:23.555 --> 00:15:25.807
You guys are winning too much.

00:15:26.015 --> 00:15:29.310
Many businessmen are involved
with that competition.

00:15:29.519 --> 00:15:32.856
There's a lot, <i>a Iot,</i> of money in it.

00:15:33.064 --> 00:15:37.193
So there's a certain...
Yes, there's a system.

00:15:37.402 --> 00:15:40.363
You 're saying l 'm winning too much,
and some people are losing money?

00:15:40.572 --> 00:15:44.242
You 're sharp. Really sharp!

00:15:44.451 --> 00:15:49.122
So now you get it, right?
You 're going to take part in our system.

00:15:49.330 --> 00:15:51.791
In other words, rigged matches.

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:56.713
Who knows? But as things stand,
you 're looking at 50 years in jail.

00:15:56.921 --> 00:15:59.883
Pifty years would be a problem. l 'll cooperate.

00:16:00.091 --> 00:16:01.259
Good.

00:16:01.468 --> 00:16:03.803
But l also want a location
where l can go all-out.

00:16:04.012 --> 00:16:04.804
What?!

00:16:05.013 --> 00:16:06.681
Not like that arena.

00:16:06.890 --> 00:16:12.061
Pighting for my life, with far more
money in play. That kind of place.

00:16:13.480 --> 00:16:14.814
Where'd you hear that?

00:16:15.023 --> 00:16:16.816
It's how things work in this field.

00:16:17.025 --> 00:16:19.152
Do you know the details involved?

00:16:19.360 --> 00:16:22.363
Of course. They're illegal battles
for VIPs to watch.

00:16:22.572 --> 00:16:25.033
Using firearms loaded with live ammo.

00:16:25.241 --> 00:16:29.621
I heard it's a life-or-death combat spectacle,
on the city's outskirts.

00:16:29.829 --> 00:16:31.956
I also hear the payout is way higher.

00:16:32.165 --> 00:16:36.127
Half of those who compete are dead
within a matter of months.

00:16:36.336 --> 00:16:38.129
Are you also aware of that?

00:16:38.338 --> 00:16:40.298
That sounds about right.

00:16:44.302 --> 00:16:45.970
Should l ask what your motive is?

00:16:46.179 --> 00:16:47.013
Money.

00:16:47.222 --> 00:16:48.348
Anything else?

00:16:48.556 --> 00:16:50.266
I 'm out for blood.

00:16:52.977 --> 00:16:55.313
Pine, then. l ' ll talk to the right people.

00:16:55.522 --> 00:17:00.777
But until it's all done,
l 'm gonna keep your friend in custody.

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:10.620
Sousuke!

00:17:11.829 --> 00:17:14.457
What's going on? Where's Lemon?

00:17:15.416 --> 00:17:19.128
Still in jail. l talked to
the police chief and got released.

00:17:19.337 --> 00:17:22.799
The chief. You mean that scoundrel?

00:17:23.007 --> 00:17:25.176
I 'll tell you later. Let's go.

00:17:27.262 --> 00:17:29.764
Rigged matches. That figures.

00:17:29.973 --> 00:17:31.391
You 're not angry?

00:17:32.976 --> 00:17:36.646
Not really. l 'd heard rumors about it,
and you 'd have to be an idiot

00:17:36.854 --> 00:17:39.899
to expect sportsmanship
in a city like this, right?

00:17:40.108 --> 00:17:42.735
But isn 't it weird that he
released you so readily?

00:17:42.944 --> 00:17:44.529
I demanded a certain condition.

00:17:44.737 --> 00:17:45.863
Condition?

00:17:46.072 --> 00:17:46.990
Illegal battles.

00:17:47.198 --> 00:17:48.199
Illegal battles?!

00:17:48.408 --> 00:17:50.868
Do you realize what you 're getting into?

00:17:51.077 --> 00:17:52.579
Real fighting, with live ammo.

00:17:52.787 --> 00:17:55.498
Serious mortal combat.
The money's good, too.

00:17:55.707 --> 00:17:59.168
You 'd use that machine of mine
for a death match?!

00:17:59.377 --> 00:18:03.172
Get real! Those battles are
the absolute last option

00:18:03.381 --> 00:18:06.301
for some idiot who's deep in debt!

00:18:06.509 --> 00:18:09.262
We' re not like that!
We' re nearly up to Class A!

00:18:09.470 --> 00:18:10.972
Are you insane?!

00:18:11.180 --> 00:18:13.641
Explain why you ' re doing this!

00:18:13.850 --> 00:18:15.184
Well...

00:18:16.811 --> 00:18:18.187
You can 't tell me?

00:18:18.396 --> 00:18:23.901
Look, l thought we were
at least friends at this point.

00:18:24.110 --> 00:18:25.486
Was l wrong?

00:18:25.695 --> 00:18:28.990
I don 't want to die not knowing anything.

00:18:34.704 --> 00:18:35.580
Nami.

00:18:35.788 --> 00:18:38.750
You 're right. Thank you. l 'll explain.

00:18:40.501 --> 00:18:41.711
Have a seat.

00:18:45.006 --> 00:18:48.134
My objective was
the illegal battles from the start.

00:18:48.343 --> 00:18:50.803
To get closer to the dark side of the operation,

00:18:51.012 --> 00:18:54.015
l needed to keep winning the public battles.

00:18:54.223 --> 00:18:56.059
Y-Yeah, but what for?

00:18:56.267 --> 00:18:59.812
Because apparently, Amalgam is
involved with the illegal battles.

00:19:00.021 --> 00:19:02.482
Amalgam...?

00:19:02.690 --> 00:19:04.400
It's the name of an organization.

00:19:04.609 --> 00:19:08.071
They plan and stage conflicts
all around the world.

00:19:08.279 --> 00:19:10.531
They've played a role in
the serious terrorist incidents

00:19:10.740 --> 00:19:12.784
that occurred over the past several years.

00:19:12.992 --> 00:19:15.203
H-Hold on...

00:19:15.411 --> 00:19:19.165
There's a top-secret mercenary force
that was fighting against Amalgam.

00:19:19.374 --> 00:19:21.542
I 'm a survivor of that force.

00:19:21.751 --> 00:19:23.753
Survivor?

00:19:23.961 --> 00:19:26.255
What happened to it, then?

00:19:26.464 --> 00:19:30.510
It was wiped out by Amalgam.
Three months ago.

00:19:30.718 --> 00:19:32.178
No way...

00:19:32.387 --> 00:19:35.014
Amalgam is an organization
hidden in the shadows.

00:19:35.223 --> 00:19:37.850
On my own, it's hard to even contact them.

00:19:38.059 --> 00:19:42.021
The few clues l have are this city
and the illegal battles.

00:19:42.230 --> 00:19:46.150
We've defeated Amalgam ASes
several times in the past.

00:19:46.359 --> 00:19:49.737
We recovered the bodies of
the operators and identified them.

00:19:49.946 --> 00:19:52.699
Several of them had been competitors <i>here.</i>

00:19:52.907 --> 00:19:54.701
At this arena?

00:19:54.909 --> 00:19:56.619
Of that much l 'm sure.

00:19:56.828 --> 00:20:00.331
But my group was destroyed
before we could investigate further.

00:20:00.540 --> 00:20:01.874
Are you for real?

00:20:02.083 --> 00:20:03.543
Affirmative.

00:20:03.751 --> 00:20:07.422
Well, l did think your skills
were extraordinary.

00:20:07.630 --> 00:20:11.426
In that case, aren't those guys
total bad news?

00:20:11.634 --> 00:20:16.180
That's right. l want to get close to Amalgam.

00:20:16.389 --> 00:20:18.891
Por that, l need your cooperation.

00:20:22.145 --> 00:20:23.604
Screw that!

00:20:24.647 --> 00:20:25.648
Na--

00:20:26.816 --> 00:20:28.443
Go make war by yourself!

00:20:28.651 --> 00:20:30.737
It has nothing to do with me!

00:20:32.029 --> 00:20:33.948
Wait! Listen to me!

00:20:34.157 --> 00:20:37.410
You 're fired! Never show
your face around here again.

00:20:42.165 --> 00:20:43.958
Well, that figures.

00:21:21.120 --> 00:21:22.497
Nami!

00:21:22.705 --> 00:21:24.916
What're you doing?

00:21:25.124 --> 00:21:26.501
Being careful.

00:21:28.920 --> 00:21:31.214
There's something l at least want to ask you.

00:21:31.422 --> 00:21:32.173
What?

00:21:32.381 --> 00:21:34.217
You 're in a bind, aren 't you?

00:21:34.425 --> 00:21:35.218
Yeah.

00:21:35.426 --> 00:21:37.011
You need my help?

00:21:37.220 --> 00:21:38.513
Affirmative.

00:21:40.223 --> 00:21:44.101
All right. l ' ll go along with this for a bit.

00:21:45.102 --> 00:21:46.187
You 're sure?

00:21:46.395 --> 00:21:51.150
Lemon 's in prison, and all.
And the fight money's good, right?

00:21:51.359 --> 00:21:52.610
Well, yes.

00:21:52.819 --> 00:21:55.488
Just don't expect too much.

00:21:55.696 --> 00:21:58.825
I don 't know if Asch and the others
will go along with it.

00:21:59.033 --> 00:22:00.993
If they all say no, then it's no.

00:22:01.202 --> 00:22:02.537
Understood.

00:22:03.788 --> 00:22:05.540
He doesn 't seem to be making a run for it.

00:22:05.748 --> 00:22:07.875
Apparently, he's serious
about the illegal battles.

00:22:08.084 --> 00:22:09.418
I bet he is.

00:22:09.627 --> 00:22:11.379
Keep an <i>eye</i> on him, though.

00:22:11.587 --> 00:22:12.672
Yes, sir.

00:22:15.132 --> 00:22:16.384
It's me.

00:22:17.844 --> 00:22:20.096
P-Pardon me, sir!

00:22:20.304 --> 00:22:22.723
N-No, l would never dream <i>of...</i>

00:22:23.891 --> 00:22:27.144
Yes, sir. He'll never get away.

00:22:27.353 --> 00:22:28.938
So please, rest assured.

00:22:29.146 --> 00:22:32.567
Rest assured? l can 't do that.

00:22:32.775 --> 00:22:36.028
You 'd best take Sousuke Sagara seriously.

00:22:36.237 --> 00:22:39.949
I am fully aware of that, Mr. Kurama.

00:22:40.157 --> 00:22:40.908
Are you now?

00:22:41.117 --> 00:22:42.535
Yes, sir! You have--

00:22:45.162 --> 00:22:47.915
I just knew he'd come find us.

